Package: QBL
Type: Package
Title: Quantitative Bayesian Lasso for Bivariate Haplotype Association
Version: 1.0.0
Author: Ibrahim Hossain Sajal, Swati Biswas, Shili Lin
Maintainer: Ibrahim Hossain Sajal <ihossain2@isrt.ac.bd>
Description: Implements quantitative Bayesian lasso for haplotype association analysis with two correlated continuous phenotypes. Takes a dataset containing the two phenotypes and SNP genotypes, with no environmental covariates. Uses Markov chain Monte Carlo sampling to estimate posterior distributions of regression coefficients and haplotype frequencies. Provides posterior means, credible intervals, and Bayes factors for individual haplotype and overall haplotype association.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0), hapassoc
Imports: stats
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: yes
